# Feature Branch

When starting work on a new feature (e.g. from backlog, user request, or plan):

1. Create a feature branch first: `git checkout -b feature/kebab-case-name`
2. Use kebab-case for the branch name (e.g. `feature/kite-command`, `feature/border-damage-immunity`)
3. On Windows PowerShell, use `;` instead of `&&` to chain commands (e.g. `cd path; git checkout -b feature/name`)

Do not begin implementing until the branch is created.
